{"baseRefName":"main","body":"Update every detected ecosystem, including release tooling, experiment projects, language runtimes, Actions and pre-commit hooks. Regenerate npm/Cargo locks and add universal hash-locked Python and NuGet restores. Align parser releases to the latest available in each registry: 0.31.5 for npm/PyPI/crates, 0.31.1 for NuGet.\n\nFixes #86\n\n- Fix the JavaScript release's remote manifest lookup. Reproduce by running the release version check from `js/` against a branch with a different root manifest version; `js/scripts/package-version.test.mjs` verifies it reads the JS package.\n- Extend freshness checks, audits and Dependabot across the repository. Preserve strict Python checks and all existing codec tests; migrate annotations, formatting and Rust let chains for current tools. Universal Python locking includes Windows-only dependencies.\n- Replace fetched/evaluated release loaders with shared locked packages and native regex/string APIs; remove the obsolete npm-11 selector. Add major release fragments for the raised runtime floors.\n- Trace real locked C# builds in CodeQL manual mode: the current buildless extractor fails .NET 11 restores despite a successful scan conclusion. The reusable restore reproduction and CI verify the workaround.\n\nValidation: JavaScript 596 tests; 122 shared/release-script tests; Python 536 tests, strict mypy, Ruff, pre-commit, wheel/sdist/twine; Rust all-features/no-default-features tests, doctests, Clippy, formatting, release build and all experiment projects; .NET 541 tests, coverage, release build, formatting, pack and consumers. Freshness checks cover 234 direct declarations. JavaScript, Python, all six Cargo locks and .NET audits report no known vulnerabilities. The separate root npm CLI audit remains blocked as described below.\n\n**Unfinished acceptance criteria / external blockers:** npm 12.2.2 is the latest official release but bundles vulnerable glob 13.0.6 and minimatch 10.2.5 (two reviewed advisories, 21 propagated moderate audit findings). Consumer overrides do not replace its bundled copies. The strict audit remains enabled and fails explicitly; no claim of zero unresolved advisories or entirely green PR CI is made. A fixed upstream CLI release is required. Separately, default-branch PyPI publishing fails with `invalid-publisher` until a PyPI account owner configures the existing Trusted Publisher runbook. Default-branch code also cannot change until this PR is merged by its owner. Keep the PR unmerged and these criteria unfinished.\n\nUpstream reports (necessary workarounds retained): [npm CLI bundled advisories](https://github.com/npm/cli/issues/10299#issuecomment-6879318834), [Python parser typing marker](https://github.com/link-foundation/links-notation/issues/411), [Scriv's exact dependency pins](https://github.com/nedbat/scriv/issues/209#issuecomment-6878955200), [meta-language's published parser dependencies](https://github.com/link-foundation/meta-language/issues/197#issuecomment-6878955660), [lino-env's published parser dependencies](https://github.com/link-foundation/lino-env/issues/33#issuecomment-6878956084), [actionlint concurrency queue support](https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint/pull/654#issuecomment-6879054277), [CodeQL .NET 11 restore](https://github.com/github/codeql/issues/23133).\n\nThe complete requirement map, registry-backed before/latest/after tables, migration review, exceptions, verification and CI evidence are in [dev/log/issues/86/pulls/87](https://github.com/link-foundation/lino-objects-codec/tree/issue-86-35430a936d8f/dev/log/issues/86/pulls/87).\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOQWrSmc8AAAABmhC4fg","author":{"login":"konard"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Final verification for `879260f01453da043869be3f8879b9f236821a06` (runs created 2026-11-14 15:25:42 UTC): every run has finished. This is the final receipt for the last step in the archived work plan.\n\n| Workflow | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| [JavaScript](https://github.com/link-foundation/lino-objects-codec/actions/runs/43610124331) | Pass |\n| [Python, including Windows](https://github.com/link-foundation/lino-objects-codec/actions/runs/43610124291) | Pass |\n| [Rust](https://github.com/link-foundation/lino-objects-codec/actions/runs/43610124319) | Pass |\n| [C#](https://github.com/link-foundation/lino-objects-codec/actions/runs/43610124263) | Pass |\n| [Dependency freshness](https://github.com/link-foundation/lino-objects-codec/actions/runs/43610124255) | Pass |\n| [Workflow lint/security](https://github.com/link-foundation/lino-objects-codec/actions/runs/43610124276) | Pass |\n| [Shared scripts](https://github.com/link-foundation/lino-objects-codec/actions/runs/43610124231) | Pass |\n| [Cross-language parity](https://github.com/link-foundation/lino-objects-codec/actions/runs/43610124304) | Pass |\n| [Links](https://github.com/link-foundation/lino-objects-codec/actions/runs/43610124191) | Pass |\n| [Security](https://github.com/link-foundation/lino-objects-codec/actions/runs/43610124310) | **Blocked: npm CLI audit only** |\n\nThe complete failed Security log was downloaded and reviewed. In `security-43610124310.log`, line 1333 reports 21 propagated moderate findings from two advisories in the latest official npm 12.2.2 bundle; line 1340 confirms the separate JS application audit has zero findings; line 1341 preserves the explicit nonzero failure. Every other security job passes. C# CodeQL traces successful locked builds at lines 11753, 11764 and 11775. The [npm upstream report](https://github.com/npm/cli/issues/10299#issuecomment-6879318834) documents why consumer overrides cannot repair its bundled copies. No audit is suppressed.\n\nThe second unfinished acceptance criterion is completely green default-branch publishing: main's [Python release](https://github.com/link-foundation/lino-objects-codec/actions/runs/43602367955) is rejected with `invalid-publisher`. A PyPI account owner must configure the Trusted Publisher (owner `link-foundation`, repository `lino-objects-codec`, workflow `python.yml`, environment empty). The existing preflight and runbook explain this; editing this PR cannot supply foreign account authority.\n\nLocal full validation includes 596 JS tests, 122 release/shared script tests, 536 Python tests, 119 Rust tests plus 9 doctests, and 541 .NET tests, alongside builds, lint, typing, packaging, consumers and audits. The [evidence folder](https://github.com/link-foundation/lino-objects-codec/tree/issue-86-35430a936d8f/dev/log/issues/86/pulls/87) contains all 24 requirement groups, registry-backed dependency tables, 91 explained retained resolutions, migration reviews, reproductions and seven upstream reports. Final-SHA logs and receipts are also preserved locally under that folder's `ci-logs/`.\n\nThe final commit adds research/evidence only; reviewed source is unchanged from `df9435e`. `gh pr diff` was reviewed before the evidence commit. Afterward GitHub's 300-file diff limit required the paginated PR-files API plus local diff for final review. Main `023932f` is already incorporated; the working tree is clean; PR title/body include the actual scope, tests and `Fixes #86`. PR 87 is ready for review and remains unmerged. The two blocked acceptance criteria above remain unfinished; this is not a claim that the entire issue or native goal is complete.\n","createdAt":"2026-11-14T15:30:13Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/lino-objects-codec/pull/87#issuecomment-6879754366","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOQWrSmc8AAAABmhFUvw","author":{"login":"konard"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"## 🤖 Solution Draft Log\nThis log file contains the complete execution trace of the AI solution draft process.\n\n### 💰 **Cost estimation:**\n- Model: GPT-6.1 Sol\n- Provider: OpenAI\n- Public pricing estimate: $8.097783\n\n### 📊 **Context and tokens usage:**\n- 675.1K input tokens across requests (cumulative, larger than the 272K context window, so not one request's context), 122.7K / 128K (96%) output tokens\n\nTotal: (675.1K + 17.8M cached) input tokens, 122.7K output tokens, $8.097783 cost\n\n### 🤖 **Models used:**\n- Tool: OpenAI Codex\n- Requested: `gpt-6.1-sol`\n- Thinking level: xhigh (~31999 tokens)\n- **Model: GPT-6.1 Sol** (`gpt-6.1-sol`)\n\n### 📎 **Log file uploaded as Gist** (4564KB)\n- [View complete solution draft log](https://gist.githubusercontent.com/konard/ffceb91ecf56acdeb77a207ee34b3bd3/raw/f57cf9601dc3d1402495480520bfe8be3fa49120/tmp-hive-mind-log-upload-XFoO6O-sanitized.log.txt)\n\n---\n*Now working session is ended, feel free to review and add any feedback on the solution draft.*","createdAt":"2026-11-14T15:32:35Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/lino-objects-codec/pull/87#issuecomment-6879794367","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOQWrSmc8AAAABmhKBMA","author":{"login":"konard"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"## 🔄 Auto-restart 1/5\n\n**Reason:** CI failures detected\n\n**Evidence:**\n- Failing check: CodeQL — https://github.com/link-foundation/lino-objects-codec/runs/132495196621\n- Failing check: Audit npm lock — https://github.com/link-foundation/lino-objects-codec/actions/runs/43610749304/job/132495042293\n\nStarting a new session to address it.","createdAt":"2026-11-14T15:37:11Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/lino-objects-codec/pull/87#issuecomment-6879871280","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-11-14T14:05:48Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-11-14T14:05:48Z","messageBody":"Adding .gitkeep for PR creation (default mode).\nThis file will be removed when the task is complete.\n\nIssue: https://github.com/l